### Extract HTTP request and response using host.switchToHttp()

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/fundamentals/execution-context.md

Switch to the HTTP application context and retrieve typed request and response objects. Type arguments can be passed to getRequest and getResponse to return natively typed Express objects.

```typescript
const ctx = host.switchToHttp();
const request = ctx.getRequest<Request>();
const response = ctx.getResponse<Response>();
```

